\subsection{Fine-grained Cells in MOEDA Flow}
To further improve solutions while balancing multiple objectives, which the standard digital flow is not capable of and instead prioritises timing alone, the MOEDA flow is used to enlarge the solution space, offering a wide range of Pareto-optimised solutions. Subsequent optimisation performed by the MOEDA flow is starting from a set of solutions obtained by the standard digital flow with the ``MINI\_FINE'' library (``STD+FINE''). This is because the results of ``STD+FINE'' achieve better circuit evaluation metrics than the solution of using the ``MINI\_ORIG'' library initially, so that the MOEDA's optimisation efforts are focused on finding better trade-off solutions regarding PPA, rather than starting from scratch.

