% 5 - Our proposal
We propose \BALToR{} (\textbf{B}ounded-\textbf{A}bstention \textbf{L}earning \textbf{To} \textbf{R}ank), a novel method for abstention in pairwise learning-to-rank settings. To devise \BALToR{}, we first characterize the optimal selection strategy that determines when the ranking model should abstain from providing a relative ordering between item pairs. 
%
This strategy is based on thresholding the model’s conditional risk: the system abstains when the estimated risk exceeds a predefined threshold. Given a bound on the allowable fraction of abstentions over pairwise comparisons, \BALToR{} aims to maximize ranking performance on the remaining, non-abstained pairs.
