	\begin{lemma}\label{P_1}{\rm(\cite{A25}, Theorem 3.1)}
		Let $\ell \in \mathbb{Z}^{+}$ with $2\leq\ell<\frac{n}{2}-1$. For the q-ary MDS linear code $\mathcal{C}=[n, n-2 \ell-1, 2 \ell+2]$, if $\mathcal{C}$ has an $\ell$-error-correcting pair $(\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{B})$, then the parameters of $\mathcal{A}$ have the following three possibilities, 
