The benchmark evaluates the degree obtained by our implementation and compares it with \rc. Since the algorithm discussed in Section~\ref{sec:cert} to compute certificates of strictly positive polynomials can handle any set of generators, we use the monogenic generator $\set{(1-x^2)^{k}}$ where $k$ is an odd natural number. The semialgebraic set for this generator is the interval $[-1, 1]$. We use different values of $\epsilon > 0$ and $k$ of the strictly polynomial $(1 + \epsilon) + x $ over $\semialgebraic(\set{(1-x^2)^{k}})$ to report the degrees of the certificates obtained and the time (in second) taken in Table~\ref{tab:2} below.

