        s_{o,i}\tilde L_{i}C&s_{o,i}\tilde L_{i} & v_i(h_{o,i})^2s_{o,i}^2 
    \end{bmatrix}\succeq 0, \forall i\in\mathcal{I}(H_o),
\end{equation*}
that, recalling that $\tilde N=\tilde LS_o$, is equivalent to \eqref{eq:locality_set_dISS_obs2}.
\smallskip\\
In case $\mathcal I(H_o) =\emptyset$, the Lyapunov function $V_o(x,\hat x)$ satisfies \eqref{eq:dissipation_form_function_observer}
for all $x, \hat x\in\R^n$, $w\in\mathcal{E}(Q_w^0)$. and $\eta\in\mathcal{E}(Q_\eta^0)$. Additionally, $V_o(x,\hat x)$ satisfies $\lambda_{\min}(P_o)\norm{x-\hat x}^2\leq V_o(x,\hat x)\leq\lambda_{\max}(P_o)\norm{x-\hat x}^2$. Moreover, the functions $\alpha_1(\norm{x-\hat x})=\lambda_{\min}(P)\norm{x-\hat x}^2$, $\alpha_2(\norm{x-\hat x})=\lambda_{\max}(P_o)\norm{x-\hat x}^2$ and $\alpha_3(\norm{x-\hat x})=\norm{x-\hat x}^2_{Q_{o,x}}$ are class $\mathcal{K}_\infty$, and $\alpha_4(\norm{w_o})=\norm{w_o}^2_{Q_{o,w_o}}$ is a class $\mathcal{K}$-function. Consequently, $V_o(x,\hat x)$ is a dissipation-form $\delta$ISS function over the sets $\R^n$, $\mathcal{E}(Q_{w}^0)$, and $\mathcal{E}(Q_\eta^0)$, and by Theorem~\ref{th:local_dISS}, system \eqref{eq:observer_dynamics} is $\delta$ISS with respect to these sets.\\
Conversely, if $\mathcal I(H_o) \neq\emptyset$, the invariance of the set $\mathcal{E}(P_o/\gamma_o)$ ensures that, if the initial condition satisfies $e(0),\in\mathcal{E}(P_o/\gamma_o)$, then $e(k)\in\mathcal{E}(P_o/\gamma_o)$ for all $k>0$ . Since $\mathcal{E}(P_o/\gamma_o)\subseteq\mathcal{V}(H_o)$, and $w\in\mathcal{E}(Q_{w}^0)$ and $\eta\in\mathcal{E}(Q_\eta^0)$, it follows that $v,\hat v\in\mathcal V(H_o)$. Therefore, $V_o(x,\hat x)$ satisfies \eqref{eq:dissipation_form_function_observer}. By Theorem~\ref{th:local_dISS}, this implies that system \eqref{eq:observer_dynamics} is $\delta$ISS with respect to the sets $\mathcal{E}(P_o/\gamma_o)$, $\mathcal{E}(Q_{w}^0)$, and $\mathcal{E}(Q_\eta^0)$, concluding the proof.
\hfill{}$\square$\smallskip\\
