In view of Assumption~\ref{ass:disturbance}, condition \eqref{eq:mRPI_set_condition_1_dISS} implies $\norm{w_{c,j}}^2_{Q_{c,w_c}}\leq \norm{w_{c,j}}^2_{Q_{w_c}^0}\leq 1$. 
This implies that
\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{lcl}
V(\hat x_j^+,\bar{x})\!-\!V(\hat x_j,\bar{x})&\!\!=\!\!&\|\hat x_j^+\!-\!\bar{x}\|^2_{P_c}-\|\hat x_j\!-\!\bar{x}\|^2_{P_c}\\
&\leq&-\norm{\hat x_j-\bar{x}}^2_{Q_{c,x}}+1.\end{array}\label{eq:dissipation_form_function_4}\end{equation}
Moreover, note that applying a congruence transformation to  \eqref{eq:mRPI_set_condition_2_dISS} yields
\(Q_{c,x}-P_c/\gamma_c\succeq0\).
Therefore, since \eqref{eq:dissipation_form_function_4} and \eqref{eq:mRPI_set_condition_2_dISS} hold, it follows from Lemma~\ref{lem:RPI_set} that if $\hat x-\bar x\in\mathcal{E}(P_c/\gamma_c)$, then $\hat x^+-\bar x\in\mathcal{E}(P_c/\gamma_c)$, i.e., $\hat x^+\in\mathcal{E}(P_c/\gamma_c)\oplus\bar x$, as claimed.\smallskip\\
%
%which implies $\mathcal{E}(Q_{c,x})\oplus\bar x\subseteq\mathcal{E}(P_c/\gamma_c)\oplus\bar x$.
