Specifically, \emph{basic} curved nonograms are \change{exactly} the puzzles in which each description corresponds to a sequence of {\em distinct} faces.
%, i.e., the curve arrangement does not contain any popular faces.
The analogy with descriptions in classic nonograms is straightforward. 
In an \emph {advanced} curved nonogram, a face may be incident to the same curve multiple times, but only on the same side,
