If such a face is filled it is also counted multiple times when checking consistency with a description; in particular, it is no longer true that the sum of the numbers in a description is equal to the total number of filled faces incident to the curve.
\emph {Expert} curved nonograms may have descriptions in which a single face is incident to the same curve on \emph {both} sides (which corresponds to the presence of a self-intersecting curve in the arrangement).

