\section{Conclusion}
We propose a neural-symbolic synthesis approach, \name{}, for automatically translating tensor programs across heterogeneous deep learning systems with different programming models. \name{} conducts the program translation as a series of LLM-assisted transformation passes, where incorrect code snippets are repaired by small-scale symbolic synthesis. In addition to ensuring functional correctness, \name{} also employs hierarchical auto-tuning to improve the performance of translated programs. Experimental results on $4$ different DLS demonstrate that \name{} correctly translates different tensor programs at the accuracy of 95\% on average, and the performance of translated program achieves up to $2.0\times$ over vendor-provided manually-optimized libraries. Moreover, the programming productivity of DLS is improved by up to $96.0\times$.

