\section{Methodology}

Consider the simplified search space in Section~\ref{sec:peformancecollapse}, it can be easily inferred that the $\alpha_{skip}$, $\alpha_{conv}$, and $\alpha_{avg}$ follow:

\begin{multline}\label{eqn:alpha_conv}
    e^{\alpha_{conv}} + e^{\alpha_{skip}} + e^{\alpha_{avg}} = 2*\text{Var}(x-\overline{m} (x)) + \\ 2*\text{Var}(o_a(x)-\overline{m} (x)) + 2*\text{Var}(o_c(x)-\overline{m} (x)) - \\ 3 * \text{Cov}(x-\overline{m} (x), o_c(x)-\overline{m} (x), o_a(x)-\overline{m} (x)) + C
\end{multline}
Therefore, to reduce the overall variances, we can choose a smaller value for $\alpha$, so $\exp(\alpha)$ is small.

