\subsection{More on hyperparameters on Equation~\ref{eqn:smu}}
For most tasks, the performance of the special case in Eqn. \ref{eqn:mrloss} of regularizing mean values is not sensitive to the task type. In this work, we started with the special case mean regularizer in Eqn. \ref{eqn:mrloss} for each task which can already give us SOTA. Then we tune $vu$ in Eqn. \ref{eqn:smu} to change the slope for negative inputs, finally, we can change smoothness by tuning $mu$ in $erf$ function Eqn. \ref{eqn:smu} for more improvements.
In addition, once the $mu$ and $vu$ combination Eqn. \ref{eqn:smu} is in the optimal neighborhood, the performance is not sensitive to the change in $mu$ and $vu$. Through ablation study, we find many pairs of hyperparameters that can achieve SOTA results on NAS-Bench-201. For instance, when we set =1e6 (mimicking infinity), =0.25 or 0.75 will both achieve SOTA architecture in NASBench201 with CIFAR10 valid 91.55\%.

