\subsection{Experimental Setup}
\label{supp:didactic_setup}
We uniformly sample $N = 512$ points from $f(x)$ within the interval $[0,4.3]$ to build the training dataset. A network $G(x)$ is trained to predict an output $y_i$ that approximates $\hat{y} = f(x)$ for every $x_i$ in the dataset where $1 \leq i \leq N$. The prediction errors for the entire dataset are then aggregated into a vector,
\[
\Delta = \begin{bmatrix}
\hat{y}_1 - y_1 \\
\vdots \\
\hat{y}_N - y_N
\end{bmatrix} ,
\]
and provided as input to the discriminator $D(\Delta)$.
Both $G(x)$ and $D(\Delta)$ consist of 2 hidden layers with 1024 and 512 units, respectively. The GP weight $\lambda^{GP}$ is set to 0.1. Table \ref{tab:suppADDRegressionParams} provides a detailed documentation of the hyperparameters used in this experiment.

