\section{Problem setup}
\noindent
{Consider a bounded linear operator $\mathcal{A}_P$ on a finite dimensional Hilbert space $\mathcal{H}$. %, such that some proper cone $\mathcal{X}$ is invariant under $\mathcal{A}_P$, i.e. ${\mathcal{A}_Px\in\mathcal{X}}$ for all ${x\in\mathcal{X}}$. 
Let $\mathcal{A}_P$ be continuously parameterized by ${P\in\mathcal{P}}$, where $\mathcal{P}$ is compact. Let ${\mathcal{X}\subset{}\mathcal{H}}$ be a proper cone, and $\mathcal{A}_P$ and $h(P)$ be such that for each ${P\in\mathcal{P}}$, ${\mathcal{A}_P:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow{}\mathcal{X}}$ and ${h(P):\mathcal{P}\rightarrow{}\interior{\mathcal{X}^*}}$. We analyze the infinite-horizon optimal control problem}
