			      Edges with different colors correspond to different components\protect\sharedfootnotemark{} from the second-order perturbative reduction; see \Cref{lem:pathA} for details.
			      Note that $k$ can be \emph{polynomially} large since it only introduces a $\sqrt{k+1}$ overhead on weights.
